				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">The little dwarf went out and gathered his forces. He found some mighty warriors with very cold hearts. The crowd gathered around the dwarf, as he stood upon a rock outside of Kalidam.
<br />

<br />
"To arms my brothers and sisters, we must unite and fight the good fight!!" The mighty dwarf yelled.
<br />

<br />
The crowd let out a roar, and then began to listen to the dwarf again.
<br />

<br />
"Our mighty leader Needra has given the order that we go to war. This uncalled for offence by our once allies and freinds can not go unchecked." He spoke as he unsheathed his sword. "We must banish our foes from this land and tech them a lesson once and for all!" he yelled as he leapt off of the rock.
<br />

<br />
He walked into the crowd parting it down the middle. They collapsed and followed him until he came upon his valiant steed. He jumped up onto the horse, and slid his helmet onto his head his head. 
<br />

<br />
He slapped his horse and it began to trot off, as the heroes followed him through Butcherblock mountains.
<br />

<br />
"Sir, we have reports from our scouts that the enemy is only an hour away from our position." Callidan told General Trefellgion.
<br />

<br />
"Good, good thank you Leuitenant that will be all." The valiant warrior replied.
<br />

<br />
Trefellgion sat down in the green pastures of East commonlands. He snatched some of the grass from the ground and tossed it into the wind. He thought to himself why our former friends would war us over such a petty thing? Where was their evidence? Why was the leader "the so called peacemaker" raising arms? All good questions to be answered after we have captured and savigally interrogated their officers and their leader. 
<br />

<br />
"Sir, Sir! Our leader has given the order to start forming up." Callidan shouted at his officer as he ran towards him.
<br />

<br />
"Very well, get the troops to form up as we have already discussed."
<br />
general Trefellgion explained to his young officer.
<br />

<br />
Callidan ran off towards the troops to get them into postition for the iminent battle. 
<br />

<br />
"Warriors up front, Healers necros and shammies in the back. Wizzies you ride with me." Callidan explained to the troops.
<br />

<br />
A familiar sound of hoofs punded the ground as the troops arose one by one as their glorious leader rode by on her horse. Raveena was what one would expect in a leader; smart, patient, strong, and charismatic. She stroked the silver main on her horse as she flipped her shiny orange hair out of her eyes. She looked up at the troops and smiled.
<br />

<br />
"My fellow guildmates, I have always tried to stress the importance of a good relationship with other guilds. I have stressed that we be good and fair people. Apparently we have not, and for this we get to charge into battle for nothing. Well I shouldn't say for nothing. We go to battle to fight for all the unjust and wrongdoings that have been held before us. I leave you with these words; No matter what happens out there today i am pround of you all for fighting the good fight and being true to what we beleive is right." She explained to her troops as they got ready to do battle.
<br />

<br />
The horns of battle sounded, as the flags of the wolf swayed in the wind above the army. The troops lined up and readied themselves for battle. the enemy appeared on the horizon, as horns could be heard in the distance.
<br />

<br />
"500 peices of platnum for every kill, 1000 peices for an officer, and 10000 peices for the head of Needra." kaandy said as she nudge Jabekaz the scaled ikky shadowknight.
<br />

<br />
"Your on, just be ready to pay me a load of coin after. if you skip out on it I swear i will hunt you down, tie you up, and play with you for months." jabekaz stated as he licked his lips. 
<br />

<br />
"Not a problem," Kaandy laughed. "I will beat you hands down."
<br />

<br />
The enemy army approached, as thundering footsteps and clanking armor could be heard. They abbruptly stopped some distance from the wolves. 
<br />

<br />
Trefellgion and Raveena sat upon their horses waiting and waiting for callidan to get into position. They rode down their line of woves as the troops stood up as the leaders passed them. They gazed up into the sky and saw a single blast of red light. That was the signal, the signal to charge to victory. 
<br />

<br />
The army of wolves charged down the grassy plains to either meet their doom or to live to fight another day. The two armies clashed with a thundering boom as steel clashed against steel. The troops fought and fought and fought, but the opposing Wuden troops were just too powerfull for them
<br />

<br />
"Take out their clerics!!" trefellgion yelled at his troops. 
<br />

<br />
Jabekaz and Ugloth arose out of the melee to find themselves looking at the mighty cerics casting. Jabekaz ran into their lines with no fear brandishing his mighty two handed sword. He swung it every what way sliceing the clerics up blood splattered every what way. Ugloth was stabbing and cleaving them, as organs and chunks of flesh were clinging to his armor. They continued to run though the line until half of the once proud line of clerics had been butchered. 
<br />

<br />
"That's it keep it up, we are breaking them!" Raveena shouted as she yanked her sword from what was once a live body.
<br />

<br />
Where was Needra in all of this? Kaandy thought to herself. Was she too frightened to fight, or is it that she knew she had done the wrong thing? i don't know and I don't care, she must pay for her evil wrong-doings. Kaandy let out a little hobbit roar as she smashed the skull of a Wudan monk with her mighty hammer. A huge palidan charged toward her swinging his sword and yelling at the hobbit. She uttered some strange words, as ice began to form on the tips of her fingers. Ice rapidly shot out of her fingers and blasted the poor palidan freezing him in a running position.
<br />

<br />
"This is just too easy, these Wuden bitches need to brush up on their fighting skills." Kaandy uttered to herself.
<br />

<br />
Out of the trees came Calidan and his mass of Wizzies, they rode like the wind charging into the rear of the Wuden army. Calidan had the look of revenge and murder in his eyes as he obliterated Wunden troop after Wuden troop.
<br />

<br />
"Mam, the troops are breaking we must pull back and regroup." The Young Dwarf said. 
<br />

<br />
"No, we must teach these scum a lesson about the ethics of rotation." Needra yelled.
<br />

<br />
Needra was not a pretty thing to look at. Shiveled up skin from all the years she had behind her. Eyes like the devil himself, mattered hair from god knows what, and a black-ice cold heart. 
<br />

<br />
"Come little dwarf we must help the troops rape these fools who dare oppose us."  Needra stated as she charged into the battle. 
<br />

<br />
Allyssia, the proud elven, was standing behind the melee scouting for possible victims with her almond shaped elven eyes. She peered from west to east as she cocked her bow with an arrow. Out of the melee somehow she had spotted the enemy leader chargeing up on  her black horse. She pulled back on her bow string and let it go, the arrow zipped though the air and peirced the horse in the breast causing it to throw the rider to the ground. 
<br />

<br />
Trefellgion turned around to see needra lieing in the grass, he waved his sword in the air and charged at her. Needra Air elemental pet greeted the genergal before he could get to the hated one. It rooted him to the gorund and began to beat on him. Needra stood up and laughed mynically at the general as he held her staff up to Trefellgion head.
<br />

<br />
"Say goodbye you foolish elf!!" Needra yelled as she uttered some strange words.
<br />

<br />
 A sword came down upon the staff, shattering it out of Needras hands. It was Wickedness coming out of the blood bath to save his general. He quickly turned around to gut an enemy troop trying to save his leader. The big ogre shadowknight threw a punch towards Needra. The heavy Iron glove caught her in the face, shattering her nose. Wickedness then turned to finish her off when she dissapeared into thin air.
<br />

<br />
Callidan was slaughtering th Wudan scum when he saw Needra all bloodied and dirty appear before him. He uttered some words and pointed his fingers at her as a huge surge of lightning shot out at her. it surged though her body as she fell to her knees.
<br />

<br />
"No..... this can't be happening...... it wasn't susspossed to happen like this" Needra mummbled.
<br />

<br />
"This is for all the good left in the world and what I beleive in -- Truth and justice." Callidan yelled as he pulled a dagger from his belt.
<br />

<br />
He sliced into the leaders neck as blood splurted out everywhere. The enrgaed wizzy then grabbed her hair abd began to yank her hair up. A loud tearing sound could be heard as callidan wrenched her head from her body. Her lifeless body fell to the ground with a thud. He held up the head as blood trickled down his arm.
<br />

<br />
"Look at what has become of your pure leader!!!" Callidan yelled as he held the head up high.
<br />

<br />
Thw Wuden army gasped in astonishment at the head of their leader. How could this have happened? No one can beat us they thought. They dropped their weapons and quickly ran towards the horizon.
<br />

<br />
"Brothers and sisters, we have won a glorious abttle for the side of good." Callidan yelped.
<br />

<br />
A huge cheer went up as the wolves raised their arms in victory.
<br />

<br />
"That's 27000 peices of platnum you owe me hobbit." Jabekaz said as he nudge the short hobbit.
<br />

<br />
"Not so fast, you owe me 48000 peices of platnum ikky." kaandy replied.
<br />

<br />
"Well how about we take the coin and go get smashed in Plane of Knowledge, your buying the first round hobbit!" Jabekaz explained.
<br />

<br />
"I will drink you under the table Ikky!" Kaandy said as she nudge the scaled humonoid.
<br />

<br />
